(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #109. On 0.4.14, `Statement::Free` for a list only
 looked the name up in the local stack frame table, so a global - which
 lives in a gvar_N BSS mirror - got no branch at all and Free was a silent
 no-op. Fixed: the global mirror is reached the same way `Free` on a global
 buffer already reaches it.)

a list called nums is [1, 2, 3].
Free nums.
print nums's length.
print nums's empty.
print nums.
append 9 to nums.
On error print "append to freed list refused".
print nums's length.
print nums.
